{"tool_name":"metaomics","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"MetaOmics","home":"https://github.com/metaOmics/metaOmics","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Analysis pipeline and browser-based software suite for transcriptomic meta-analysis.","addition_date":"2019-08-04T08:15:31Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:06:07.841216Z","tool_type":["Suite"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:MetaOmics","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"ctseng@pitt.edu","name":"George C. Tseng","typeEntity":"Person"}],"documentation":[{"note":"Tutorial material","type":["Training material"],"url":"http://nbviewer.jupyter.org/github/metaOmics/tutorial/blob/master/metaOmics_turtorial.pdf"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/metaOmics/metaOmics/blob/master/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3501"},{"term":"Expression correlation analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3463"},{"term":"Weighted correlation network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3766"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"MetaOmics","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bty825","metadata":{"abstract":"The rapid advances of omics technologies have generated abundant genomic data in public repositories and effective analytical approaches are critical to fully decipher biological knowledge inside these data. Meta-analysis combines multiple studies of a related hypothesis to improve statistical power, accuracy and reproducibility beyond individual study analysis. To date, many transcriptomic meta-analysis methods have been developed, yet few thoughtful guidelines exist. Here, we introduce a comprehensive analytical pipeline and browser-based software suite, called MetaOmics, to meta-analyze multiple transcriptomic studies for various biological purposes, including quality control, differential expression analysis, pathway enrichment analysis, differential co-expression network analysis, prediction, clustering and dimension reduction. The pipeline includes many public as well as >10 in-house transcriptomic meta-analytic methods with datadriven and biological-aim-driven strategies, hands-on protocols, an intuitive user interface and step-by-step instructions.","authors":[{"name":"Chang L.-C."},{"name":"Fang Z."},{"name":"Huo Z."},{"name":"Kim S."},{"name":"Kuo A."},{"name":"Li J."},{"name":"Lin C.-W."},{"name":"Liu P."},{"name":"Liu S."},{"name":"Ma T."},{"name":"Oesterreich S."},{"name":"Park Y."},{"name":"Rahman T."},{"name":"Sibille E."},{"name":"Song C."},{"name":"Tseng G.C."},{"name":"Wang L."},{"name":"Zeng X."},{"name":"Zhu L."}],"citationCount":19,"date":"2019-05-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"MetaOmics: Analysis pipeline and browser-based software suite for transcriptomic meta-analysis"},"pmcid":"PMC6499246","pmid":"30304367","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"MetaOmics","home":"https://bio.tools/MetaOmics","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Analysis pipeline and browser-based software suite for transcriptomic meta-analysis.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:metaomics/suite/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{}